          Type: (string) (len=9) "paragraph",
          Value: (string) (len=613) "Raiola was known for his tough negotiation tactics and for frequently defending his clients from criticism. He often used the media to attack pundits and managers, such as Paul Scholes, and in one instance referred to Pep Guardiola by saying, \"as a person he's an absolute zero. He's a coward, a dog\". Dutch journalist Taco van den Velde attributed his success to his hard work and intelligence, and his ability to fight for what was best for his client. Raiola described himself as an \"altruist\" in contrast to fellow agent Jorge Mendes, who he described as an \"egoist\", due to the differing motivations of both.",
